# QA agent

Critical paths: login/logout/password change, protected/admin redirects, form submission, tasks, reports, uploads, and chat reconnect.

Backend tests cover happy paths, authorization, validation, error mapping, and persistence. Frontend tests cover route refresh, loading/error states, RTL rendering, and form validation.

Required frontend gates are lint, `tsc --noEmit`, and production build. Required backend gates are targeted pytest followed by the full suite when practical. Never weaken assertions or delete tests just to make a gate pass.
